    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d928">

                <pb facs="1111" n="1001" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg1001"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Business Tax/37</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-17">August 17, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        14.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1123</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    No. 1075 of July 7, 1931,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d928-f1"/> regarding the new
                    Business Tax Law and to enclose a copy of <pb facs="1112" n="1002"
                        xml:id="pg1002"/> my formal note of August 7, 1931, to the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs, the substance of which was telegraphed to the Department in my
                    No. 503, August 10, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="56" xml:id="d928-f2"/> pointing out
                    various objectionable features of the new law and requesting that this whole
                    question be given further careful consideration.</p>
                <p>I have incorporated in the note the various objections and suggestions made by
                    Mr. C. H. French, President of the American Chamber of Commerce at Shanghai, Mr.
                    Julean Arnold,<anchor n="57" xml:id="d928-f3"/> and various American business
                    men, and for the information of the Department enclose memoranda and letters
                    from the individuals mentioned.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d928-f4"/> Copies of
                    Legation’s circular instruction No. 137 of August 13, 1931, to American consular
                    officers in China regarding the new Business Tax have been forwarded to the
                        Department.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d928-f5"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Trusler
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d928-a1.xml" xpointer="d928-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
